# Settings Screen — Structure Review

## Problem

The file `src/screens/settings/Settings.tsx` contains **three React components** in a single file:

1. `SettingsItem`
2. `SignOutButton`
3. `Settings` (the screen)

This violates **Rule 1: One component per file**. Each component must live in its own file.

---

## How to Fix It

Both `SettingsItem` and `SignOutButton` are only used by the `Settings` screen, so they belong as **screen fragments** under `src/screens/settings/fragments/`.

### Target file structure

```
src/screens/settings/
├── Settings.tsx
├── index.ts
└── fragments/
    ├── index.ts
    ├── settings-item/
    │   ├── SettingsItem.tsx
    │   └── index.ts
    └── sign-out-button/
        ├── SignOutButton.tsx
        └── index.ts
```

---

### `src/screens/settings/fragments/settings-item/SettingsItem.tsx`

```tsx
import React from 'react';
import { TouchableOpacity, Text, StyleSheet } from 'react-native';

export const SettingsItem = ({ label, onPress }: { label: string; onPress: () => void }) => (
  <TouchableOpacity style={styles.item} onPress={onPress}>
    <Text style={styles.label}>{label}</Text>
  </TouchableOpacity>
);

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  item: { padding: 16 },
  label: { fontSize: 16 },
});
```

### `src/screens/settings/fragments/settings-item/index.ts`

```ts
export * from "./SettingsItem";
```

---

### `src/screens/settings/fragments/sign-out-button/SignOutButton.tsx`

```tsx
import React from 'react';
import { TouchableOpacity, Text, StyleSheet } from 'react-native';

export const SignOutButton = ({ onPress }: { onPress: () => void }) => (
  <TouchableOpacity style={styles.signOut} onPress={onPress}>
    <Text style={styles.signOutLabel}>Sign out</Text>
  </TouchableOpacity>
);

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  signOut: { padding: 16, backgroundColor: 'red' },
  signOutLabel: { color: 'white' },
});
```

### `src/screens/settings/fragments/sign-out-button/index.ts`

```ts
export * from "./SignOutButton";
```

---

### `src/screens/settings/fragments/index.ts`

```ts
export * from "./settings-item";
export * from "./sign-out-button";
```

---

### `src/screens/settings/Settings.tsx`

```tsx
import React from 'react';
import { View, StyleSheet } from 'react-native';
import { SettingsItem, SignOutButton } from './fragments';

export const Settings = () => {
  return (
    <View style={styles.container}>
      <SettingsItem label="Profile" onPress={() => {}} />
      <SettingsItem label="Notifications" onPress={() => {}} />
      <SignOutButton onPress={() => {}} />
    </View>
  );
};

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: { flex: 1 },
});
```

### `src/screens/settings/index.ts`

```ts
export * from "./Settings";
```

---

## Summary of violations fixed

| Violation | Rule | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `SettingsItem` defined in `Settings.tsx` | Rule 1: one component per file | Extracted to `fragments/settings-item/SettingsItem.tsx` |
| `SignOutButton` defined in `Settings.tsx` | Rule 1: one component per file | Extracted to `fragments/sign-out-button/SignOutButton.tsx` |
| No fragment folder structure | Rule 2: screen-specific components go in `fragments/` | Created proper fragment folders with `index.ts` barrel files |

Each component's styles travel with it into its own file — there is no shared stylesheet to extract since none of the style definitions are reused across components.
